Review of docs/stateful-environments-plan.md found gaps in checkpoint
integrity, reset timing, mutating GitHub polls, and cleanup after poll
exceptions. Focused reproductions confirmed each gap before the fixes.

Checkpoint directory version 2 hashes the complete frozen tree because
checking the entry file alone cannot detect changed dependencies. The
encrypted checkpoint document stays at version 1. Older directories must
be recreated from the source world.

Running the rewritten README examples exposed two additional defects:
Webclip's corpus expected an object around a text response, and repeated
corpus runs collided with existing world directories. Webclip pack 0.5.1
and corpus 1.0.1 record the assertion correction. Fresh world identifiers
preserve earlier evidence without changing the deterministic case seed.

Validation: pnpm run ci passed across 184 test files, with 4,100 tests
passed and 55 skipped. The scripted Webclip run scored 1 with six state
changes. All seven corpus cases passed through the command line. Serve,
checkpoint, and fork examples were also checked locally.

Live provider verification and practitioner trials remain pending, as
recorded in docs/stateful-limitations.md. No live provider run was made.
